Dear Mr Moss,

Thank you for your reply about the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews.

You asked whether the issue could be limited to decorating. We cannot say yet. The tenant reports flaking paint and also that the door catches near the top, with a rub mark on the top edge. The painting quotation we sent (Pale Finch Decorating, £186.00) covers painting only and excludes the catching. Building management also lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting. An inspection should show whether painting alone is enough.

You asked for a price before any chargeable work. We do not yet know whether the inspection itself carries a charge. Before we send anyone, please confirm one of the following:
1. Send a contractor for the inspection. If there is an inspection or call-out charge, we will tell you the price first and wait for your go-ahead.
2. Send a contractor for the inspection, and you accept the inspection charge, with a limit of £[amount] that you tell us.

Either way, no repair, painting or alteration will go ahead without a quote and your approval.

